salllll/acordlayer_messaging/commit/605f9c4da5dd10edeacdb88303e848cff9cfc76d","node_id":"C_kwDOQNZMKNoAKDYwNWY5YzRkYTVkZDEwZWRlYWNkYjg4MzAzZTg0OGNmZjljZmM3NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/commit/0dc1830948914bf93a881a87f9542457c3a87cc2","sha":"0dc1830948914bf93a881a87f9542457c3a87cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/commits/0dc1830948914bf93a881a87f9542457c3a87cc2"}],"sha":"605f9c4da5dd10edeacdb88303e848cff9cfc76d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/commits/605f9c4da5dd10edeacdb88303e848cff9cfc76d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12176405?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickmisasi","id":12176405,"login":"nickmisasi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc2NDA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/commits/0dc1830948914bf93a881a87f9542457c3a87cc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-30T19:09:27Z","email":"nick.misasi@mattermost.com","name":"Nick Misasi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-30T19:09:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Build 2025] AI Plugin Bridge (#34216)\n\n* initial commit for POC of Plugin Bridge\n\n* Updates\n\n* POC for plugin bridge\n\n* Updates from collaboration\n\n* Fixes\n\n* Refactor Plugin Bridge to use HTTP/REST instead of RPC\n\n- Remove ExecuteBridgeCall hook and Context.SourcePluginId\n- Implement HTTP-based bridge using existing PluginHTTP infrastructure\n- Add CallPlugin API method with endpoint parameter instead of method name\n- Update CallPluginBridge to construct HTTP POST requests\n- Add proper headers: Mattermost-User-Id, Mattermost-Plugin-ID\n- Use ''com.mattermost.server'' as plugin ID for core server calls\n- Update ai.go to use REST endpoint /inter-plugin/v1/completion\n- Add comprehensive spec documentation in server/spec.md\n- Add MIGRATION_GUIDE.md for plugin developers\n- Fix 401/404 issues by setting correct headers and URL paths\n\n* Improve Plugin Bridge security and architecture\n\n- Create ServeInternalPluginRequest for internal plugin calls (core + plugin-to-plugin)\n- Move header-setting logic from CallPluginBridge to ServeInternalPluginRequest\n- Improve separation of concerns: business logic vs HTTP transport\n- Add security documentation explaining header protection\n\nSecurity Improvements:\n- ServeInternalPluginRequest is NOT exposed as HTTP route (internal only)\n- Headers (Mattermost-User-Id, Mattermost-Plugin-ID) are set by trusted server code\n- External requests cannot spoof these headers (stripped by servePluginRequest)\n- Core calls use ''com.mattermost.server'' as plugin ID for authorization\n- Plugin-to-plugin calls use real plugin ID (enforced by server)\n\nBackward Compatibility:\n- Keep ServeInterPluginRequest for existing API.PluginHTTP callers (deprecated)\n- All tests pass\n\nDocs:\n- Update spec.md with security model explanation\n- Update MIGRATION_GUIDE.md with correct header usage examples\n\n* Space\n\n* cursor please stop creating markdown files\n\n* Fix style\n\n* Fix i18n, linter\n\n* REMOVE MARKDOWN\n\n* Remove CallPlugin method from plugin API interface\n\nPer review feedback, this method is no longer needed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove CallPlugin method implementation from PluginAPI\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixes\n\n* Add AI OpenAPI spec\n\n* fix openapi spec\n\n* Use agents client (#34225)\n\n* Use agents client\n\n* Remove default agent\n\n* Fixes\n\n* fix: modify system prompts to ensure JSON is being returned\n\n* remove webapp changes\n\n* Add feature flags for rewrites and ai bridge, clean up\n\n* Remove comments that aren''t helpful\n\n* Fix i18n\n\n* Remove rewrites\n\n* Fix tests\n\n* Fix i18n\n\n* adjust i18n again\n\n* Add back translations\n\n* Remove leftover mock code\n\n* remove model file\n\n* Make the real substitutions\n\n* Include a basic invokation of the client with noop to ensure build works\n\n* Remove unneeded change\n\n* Updates from review\n\n* Fixes\n\n* Use v1.5.0 of agents plugin\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Speller <crspeller@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Felipe Martin <me@fmartingr.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"04fb71825e1eb972c0f93ba0850f0f0da832bf97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/git/trees/04fb71825e1eb972c0f93ba0850f0f0da832bf97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vatsalllll/acordlayer_messaging/git/commits/0dc1830948914bf93a881a87f9542457c3a87cc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 04fb71825e1eb972c0f93ba0850f0f0da832bf97\nparent 3da4996551631b4ca9b0c1d14d6dd07f36f12f8b\nauthor Nick Misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com> 1761851367 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1761851367 +0000\n\n[Build 2025] AI Plugin Bridge (#34216)\n\n* initial commit for POC of Plugin Bridge\n\n* Updates\n\n* POC for plugin bridge\n\n* Updates from collaboration\n\n* Fixes\n\n* Refactor Plugin Bridge to use HTTP/REST instead of RPC\n\n- Remove ExecuteBridgeCall hook and Context.SourcePluginId\n- Implement HTTP-based bridge using existing PluginHTTP infrastructure\n- Add CallPlugin API method with endpoint parameter instead of method name\n- Update CallPluginBridge to construct HTTP POST requests\n- Add proper headers: Mattermost-User-Id, Mattermost-Plugin-ID\n- Use ''com.mattermost.server'' as plugin ID for core server calls\n- Update ai.go to use REST endpoint /inter-plugin/v1/completion\n- Add comprehensive spec documentation in server/spec.md\n- Add MIGRATION_GUIDE.md for plugin developers\n- Fix 401/404 issues by setting correct headers and URL paths\n\n* Improve Plugin Bridge security and architecture\n\n- Create ServeInternalPluginRequest for internal plugin calls (core + plugin-to-plugin)\n- Move header-setting logic from CallPluginBridge to ServeInternalPluginRequest\n- Improve separation of concerns: business logic vs HTTP transport\n- Add security documentation explaining header protection\n\nSecurity Improvements:\n- ServeInternalPluginRequest is NOT exposed as HTTP route (internal only)\n- Headers (Mattermost-User-Id, Mattermost-Plugin-ID) are set by trusted server code\n- External requests cannot spoof these headers (stripped by servePluginRequest)\n- Core calls use ''com.mattermost.server'' as plugin ID for authorization\n- Plugin-to-plugin calls use real plugin ID (enforced by server)\n\nBackward Compatibility:\n- Keep ServeInterPluginRequest for existing API.PluginHTTP callers (deprecated)\n- All tests pass\n\nDocs:\n- Update spec.md with security model explanation\n- Update MIGRATION_GUIDE.md with correct header usage examples\n\n* Space\n\n* cursor please stop creating markdown files\n\n* Fix style\n\n* Fix i18n, linter\n\n* REMOVE MARKDOWN\n\n* Remove CallPlugin method from plugin API interface\n\nPer review feedback, this method is no longer needed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove CallPlugin method implementation from PluginAPI\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixes\n\n* Add AI OpenAPI spec\n\n* fix openapi spec\n\n* Use agents client (#34225)\n\n* Use agents client\n\n* Remove default agent\n\n* Fixes\n\n* fix: modify system prompts to ensure JSON is being returned\n\n* remove webapp changes\n\n* Add feature flags for rewrites and ai bridge, clean up\n\n* Remove comments that aren''t helpful\n\n* Fix i18n\n\n* Remove rewrites\n\n* Fix tests\n\n* Fix i18n\n\n* adjust i18n again\n\n* Add back translations\n\n* Remove leftover mock code\n\n* remove model file\n\n* Make the real substitutions\n\n* Include a basic invokation of the client with noop to ensure build works\n\n* Remove unneeded change\n\n* Updates from review\n\n* Fixes\n\n* Use v1.5.0 of agents plugin\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: claude[bot] <209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nickmisasi@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Speller <crspeller@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Felipe Martin <me@fmartingr.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpA7fnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlk8QAC5fW6Zsmz0RWO6CGz3MwZte\njbWC2iskYILCXEUyIlSFkygZtqqwpJdgAmVCu4/TJnJHjp28Okk129tGMnuBBY/Q\n1n8cuAkpoPVG9f3bxHc2opORTq7pmw1ymKLGym3+URXVbNSmNH3HFbihx1qh/y99\nJG+m5lgqM8wJEkWqKta7LYFfEytzssc7BKCY0g2bTSQc/9anAcBAcMs0gxOwfSLF\nv2PP1Wux2jy6rLFdpfC1Ufs+BgSMRndgjVkrwS6nyPoOPrOGY1fACAWoPvDiASyX\nLm2A68N0sVuqcOuS3Lhzu81gu/QqnzDk4UynzDqr4OxVYB/wSkEirBivPKouQlEp\n5NyWdUMWcxTjWMWOGqV+F5dxBMhYerbiVNaWciefjML61pIY45qhAArQ8WLRrPQ6\nSwAfBPQ8waB1Yh1eLoJSlaDP59fL8AASNjF5zDmiHpVTYOspmd2WqCZSx7yZ5p33\n4TP4MKE5KP4uTegd1SHegiEbtUIO2XDMkEFKeVf7GhM5ESofSXlDGhERcoXQv/iA\nFFCA1IvDdNODzOQOBuAXiiSRCuUUZ0ry95UIF4yDHWEu8fUAFdhVsiLuJeDhiGaE\n6+VoMTUtLKUOCjoUmB2s/zdryUnhGWpzzn58CbOm9rIKHari9o4wnTqXRuZDf58e\n4OJOqFFuDZCAK8i8q/W+