admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/commits/22a354d7eb69751c0519325d5de6097db9177bfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:26:46Z","email":"tuanhuydev@gmail.com","name":"tuanhuydev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:26:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Consolidate priority/type mapping into shared task-display module (#36)\n\nActiveSprintPage and MyTasks each hardcoded their own type-tag and\npriority-dot color maps, and had quietly drifted apart (EPIC was violet\nin one, purple in the other; ISSUE was sky vs. amber) despite both\nsupposedly representing the same domain semantics. taskTypeClasses/\ntaskPriorityStyle in task-display.ts are now the single source; labels\nstay local since they need each component''s own i18n instance, but are\nnow derived directly from the existing taskType.<value>/\ntaskPriority.<value> i18n keys instead of a second hardcoded map.\n\nLeft TaskItemPriority.vue (icon selection) alone — it''s a different\nconcern from color/label mapping, not a duplicate of it.","tree":{"sha":"0dcbe8af0c4645f1cba6dda2f4e741352f548a0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/trees/0dcbe8af0c4645f1cba6dda2f4e741352f548a0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/commits/22a354d7eb69751c0519325d5de6097db9177bfe","verification":{"payload":"tree 0dcbe8af0c4645f1cba6dda2f4e741352f548a0b\nparent e75ff947bdcab8af74d014b3f24c632a5e1d79a0\nauthor tuanhuydev <tuanhuydev@gmail.com> 1785335206 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785335206 +0700\n\nConsolidate priority/type mapping into shared task-display module (#36)\n\nActiveSprintPage and MyTasks each hardcoded their own type-tag and\npriority-dot color maps, and had quietly drifted apart (EPIC was violet\nin one, purple in the other; ISSUE was sky vs. amber) despite both\nsupposedly representing the same domain semantics. taskTypeClasses/\ntaskPriorityStyle in task-display.ts are now the single source; labels\nstay local since they need each component''s own i18n instance, but are\nnow derived directly from the existing taskType.<value>/\ntaskPriority.<value> i18n keys instead of a second hardcoded map.\n\nLeft TaskItemPriority.vue (icon selection) alone — it''s a different\nconcern from color/label mapping, not a duplicate of it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqag2mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkx4QABqeM44SEs6OXg9Hv3wl2hgd\nOonuVmaxzyIwoYoff+TiNfFRWjUbqI1ZoIUJvuj+svyd4BOKGFaq0SMy/+6xk9Ev\nP8Iiw8AAGszTRrccHygRyr0KDb8pgJUwbPrTBQDSCkIcXbhk7SWZfwaLNqSMa8sP\nTx1pfdFRRm29ZHcqYoFnLNh8MOxtayO32Jb3tZNfprTw1xjUl1XTNgSIyfBxNXif\ntAXqtAU6l9afvKweMwufgDY/fU2z/Fmhq6QH5woBAQ8EhneV72a9U7ViPKguNgrj\nqYGKJx5+4O5zBDYN8olaoHE+IeGyPp3DLrDunGTwrReZ1xecLCmwFCflEuGg/yEj\nCzkUqCLWrFD80nX2eY/gvseUl0x+ClzTwMCmvXvI+WnfBLV5nRzfg5nofvAKEiqn\nknwr6OWnOwkghecKNNHwAIfNiCXJFcOW/R8Yuf6H0sg5omMoe8K8Dl/tH70iQeER\nhib6PJx9LSaWo7TTGc2YBhxcYh2UdaDYERAlwzI/H/eFK2yKsaDQO8Yh1OgQz6cq\nlqsg1Qrn/0kUowLHVPGJGiBh5W4ClK1KUIcz8SupaLZbgeyyN7WAmZ50lnpfBD2j\nFF199NDEFGhFhhxQIuteSHxuKWozMDlbYanMQzD/3S9CzOnsDzYqPra9UroAyqAA\nuf6wsZEiZKAvpfsFnzhr\n=K0+1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T14:26:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXN