uydev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuanhuydev","id":68178042,"login":"tuanhuydev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTc4MDQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/commits/28e97388fddeb882b24bd6bae1b9549c58951368/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T09:09:17Z","email":"tuanhuydev@gmail.com","name":"tuanhuydev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T09:09:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Advanced backlog filter: status + priority (multi-select) (#25)\n\n* feat(backlogs): advanced status + priority filter (multi-select)\n\nAdd BacklogFilters — a dropdown with independent multi-select\ncheckbox groups for status and priority, showing an active-filter\ncount badge and a clear-all action. Wired into BacklogsPage''s\nfetchTasks as comma-separated query params, matching the backend''s\nGetTasksQueryDto parsing (mfex-api PR #60); refetches whenever either\nselection changes.\n\nAlso fixes a latent test fragility in BacklogsPage.test.ts: its\n\"no closed tasks\" assertion checked wrapper.text() as one blob, which\nhappened to accidentally match \"Closed task\" once an untranslated\ni18n key (\"taskbolt:backlogs.filters\") landed next to \"showClosed\" in\nthe DOM. Scoped the assertion to task-title elements instead.\n\nTASKBOLT-6a65066827ec988310fa8fdc\n\n* fix: resolve broken rebase onto main (duplicate fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints)\n\nThis branch was rebased onto main after #22/#23/#24 merged, which\nbrought in the useBacklogTasks composable (from #23) that BacklogsPage\ndidn''t have when this branch''s commit was originally written. The\nrebase/conflict resolution ended up keeping both the composable\ndestructure *and* the old inline fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints\nfunction declarations in the same scope — a duplicate-identifier error\nthat broke the build entirely (vue/compiler-sfc: \"Identifier\n''fetchMembersAndSprints'' has already been declared\").\n\nFix: move the status/priority filter params into useBacklogTasks\nitself (optional `filters: { statuses, priorities }`, defaulting to\nnone so TaskDetailPage''s existing call site is unaffected) instead of\nduplicating fetch logic in BacklogsPage. BacklogsPage now only\ndestructures fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints from the composable —\nno local re-declaration.\n\nVerified: pnpm lint (clean), pnpm build (clean), pnpm test (58 passing).\n\nTASKBOLT-6a65066827ec988310fa8fdc","tree":{"sha":"91bc8168a706a563365b6be713216f129f668521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/trees/91bc8168a706a563365b6be713216f129f668521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/commits/28e97388fddeb882b24bd6bae1b9549c58951368","verification":{"payload":"tree 91bc8168a706a563365b6be713216f129f668521\nparent c41327563df5096334b4138c28673bf9a7ddc585\nauthor tuanhuydev <tuanhuydev@gmail.com> 1785056957 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785056957 +0700\n\nAdvanced backlog filter: status + priority (multi-select) (#25)\n\n* feat(backlogs): advanced status + priority filter (multi-select)\n\nAdd BacklogFilters — a dropdown with independent multi-select\ncheckbox groups for status and priority, showing an active-filter\ncount badge and a clear-all action. Wired into BacklogsPage''s\nfetchTasks as comma-separated query params, matching the backend''s\nGetTasksQueryDto parsing (mfex-api PR #60); refetches whenever either\nselection changes.\n\nAlso fixes a latent test fragility in BacklogsPage.test.ts: its\n\"no closed tasks\" assertion checked wrapper.text() as one blob, which\nhappened to accidentally match \"Closed task\" once an untranslated\ni18n key (\"taskbolt:backlogs.filters\") landed next to \"showClosed\" in\nthe DOM. Scoped the assertion to task-title elements instead.\n\nTASKBOLT-6a65066827ec988310fa8fdc\n\n* fix: resolve broken rebase onto main (duplicate fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints)\n\nThis branch was rebased onto main after #22/#23/#24 merged, which\nbrought in the useBacklogTasks composable (from #23) that BacklogsPage\ndidn''t have when this branch''s commit was originally written. The\nrebase/conflict resolution ended up keeping both the composable\ndestructure *and* the old inline fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints\nfunction declarations in the same scope — a duplicate-identifier error\nthat broke the build entirely (vue/compiler-sfc: \"Identifier\n''fetchMembersAndSprints'' has already been declared\").\n\nFix: move the status/priority filter params into useBacklogTasks\nitself (optional `filters: { statuses, priorities }`, defaulting to\nnone so TaskDetailPage''s existing call site is unaffected) instead of\nduplicating fetch logic in BacklogsPage. BacklogsPage now only\ndestructures fetchTasks/fetchMembersAndSprints from the composable —\nno local re-declaration.\n\nVerified: pnpm lint (clean), pnpm build (clean), pnpm test (58 passing).\n\nTASKBOLT-6a65066827ec988310fa8fdc","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZc69CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8QoQAKLc2uJtHigkhJOtdHGDvY/E\nN6RhTv07lihGUnGvfjYMcj1hwvxIqWE4cmUpup4ow4PtMFQX/eGJ5V+lLzru9IjD\nbWZ9gKqWUtWqomo161zPvG3hf0+uzfkxrjPjevLw0H6P4hUxshNrzV1dAvnWnr2D\npnOrNjRt+sx4rQeTesx/I62DLfms/T0xb0ce/7VLJWvPKcCPCRpcJnKrOxm+nTaP\nFqjtVbC4O7Qn/nKt9P0oNV+n4/ZBDpsOQ/bOV1Yvs3RqNRlcHx9Dxsh8bKmBeH68\nyd95eG1qhbS0BoWebmp