owers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tuanhuydev","id":68178042,"login":"tuanhuydev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTc4MDQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tuanhuydev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/commits/46f1471e79a7af55f45267acdb2c826a32c127ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:44:05Z","email":"tuanhuydev@gmail.com","name":"tuanhuydev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:44:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(task-detail): responsive mobile drawer + IN_REVIEW status fix + backlog row UX (#11)\n\n* fix(task-detail): make task detail drawer responsive on mobile\n\nThe drawer''s content area was a fixed flex row: a flex-1 content column\nnext to a fixed w-58 (232px) properties rail. On mobile widths (e.g.\n375px) this left almost no room for either column, causing text\ntruncation, a cut-off comment editor toolbar, and content overflowing\nthe viewport.\n\n- Drawer width now defaults to full width below sm, keeping the\n  720px/92vw-capped desktop layout at sm and above.\n- Content column and properties rail now stack vertically (flex-col)\n  below md, and switch to the existing side-by-side layout at md and\n  above.\n- Border and scroll behavior adjusted per breakpoint so the stacked\n  mobile layout scrolls as a single column instead of clipping the\n  rail.\n\nFixes task 6a5987848afd1debb24aa04c.\n\n* fix(task-detail): force full-width drawer on mobile with !important\n\nDrawerContent''s base data-[vaul-drawer-direction=right]:w-3/4 class has\nhigher CSS specificity than a plain w-full utility, so the mobile width\noverride was silently losing and the drawer stayed at 75% width. Mark\nit important to match the existing sm: override pattern.\n\n* fix(task-status): add missing IN_REVIEW status color and translations\n\nThe frontend TaskStatus enum omitted IN_REVIEW even though the backend\nenum (mfex-api) has had it for a while, so any task in that status\nrendered an untranslated i18n key and fell back to the TODO gray dot.\nAdded the enum member, a distinct color, and en/vi translations.\n\n* feat(backlogs): click row to toggle sub-tasks, click title to open detail\n\nGrouped backlog rows (tasks with sub-tasks) previously opened the task\ndetail drawer on any row click, with expand/collapse only reachable via\nthe small chevron button. Clicking the row body now toggles the group\ninstead, while the title becomes the affordance for opening the detail\ndrawer (hover underline). Leaf-like parent rows with no sub-tasks keep\nopening on row click, since there''s nothing to toggle.\n\n* fix(backlogs): only underline title when the group has sub-tasks\n\nThe toggle/open split only makes sense when there''s something to\ntoggle. Rows with zero sub-tasks now look and behave exactly like a\nplain TaskItem — no hover underline on the title, since row click\nalready opens detail directly in that case.","tree":{"sha":"1c847bd9802562938407ce980fee1505fa03f3a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/trees/1c847bd9802562938407ce980fee1505fa03f3a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tuanhuydev/taskbolt/git/commits/46f1471e79a7af55f45267acdb2c826a32c127ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c847bd9802562938407ce980fee1505fa03f3a5\nparent 26d74791edd6fdab635bd067f9d5a7c259b5f7f6\nauthor tuanhuydev <tuanhuydev@gmail.com> 1784465045 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784465045 +0700\n\nfix(task-detail): responsive mobile drawer + IN_REVIEW status fix + backlog row UX (#11)\n\n* fix(task-detail): make task detail drawer responsive on mobile\n\nThe drawer''s content area was a fixed flex row: a flex-1 content column\nnext to a fixed w-58 (232px) properties rail. On mobile widths (e.g.\n375px) this left almost no room for either column, causing text\ntruncation, a cut-off comment editor toolbar, and content overflowing\nthe viewport.\n\n- Drawer width now defaults to full width below sm, keeping the\n  720px/92vw-capped desktop layout at sm and above.\n- Content column and properties rail now stack vertically (flex-col)\n  below md, and switch to the existing side-by-side layout at md and\n  above.\n- Border and scroll behavior adjusted per breakpoint so the stacked\n  mobile layout scrolls as a single column instead of clipping the\n  rail.\n\nFixes task 6a5987848afd1debb24aa04c.\n\n* fix(task-detail): force full-width drawer on mobile with !important\n\nDrawerContent''s base data-[vaul-drawer-direction=right]:w-3/4 class has\nhigher CSS specificity than a plain w-full utility, so the mobile width\noverride was silently losing and the drawer stayed at 75% width. Mark\nit important to match the existing sm: override pattern.\n\n* fix(task-status): add missing IN_REVIEW status color and translations\n\nThe frontend TaskStatus enum omitted IN_REVIEW even though the backend\nenum (mfex-api) has had it for a while, so any task in that status\nrendered an untranslated i18n key and fell back to the TODO gray dot.\nAdded the enum member, a distinct color, and en/vi translations.\n\n* feat(backlogs): click row to toggle sub-tasks, click title to open detail\n\nGrouped backlog rows (tasks with sub-tasks) previously opened the task\ndetail drawer on any row click, with expand/collapse only reachable via\nthe small chevron button. Clicking the row body now toggles the group\ninstead, while the title becomes the affordance for opening the detail\ndrawer (hover underline). Leaf-like parent rows with no sub-tasks keep\nopening on row click, since there''s nothing to toggle.\n\n* fix(backlogs): only underline title when the group has sub-tasks\n\nThe toggle/open split only makes sense when there''s something to\ntoggle. Rows with zero sub-tasks now look and behave exactly like a\nplain TaskItem — no hover underline on the title, since row click\nalready opens detail directly in that case.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXMaVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAizUQABu2kXqe3ghmaVXBXEc3BCTC\n4i5NdKQtV9frcEE+M9t2LatrAso0/6dwSCUk6omT+gKLx3cOgIIvh/Is2OH8W2v3\nv01dxmsohdVuGUnuCwaZ8UlC1K9X6qsomCevsj/TY4R3NVrBFluvVwRzihoLFrY9\na5L92PXAaf96WfJGgIifEWzgBhcF6UuIXD5ztveJLT9zm8VRjWLMrj78jcuMongC\nyDAGd2xWQKAxlc6ELHSnY2b1b7RLNzCjwX2AK1dI/fccIKme8wKXdmM+qqai3FF8\nmqEoRuqCCuaKv5uMM9KmWsefcONiHqwvK7PStz+7kbeckUG04LPoSUlqHQIHOn42\nCzD7BKWzU+lhQ3ku5ofdSKCrLO6H7Y8V7OSfxT/V2ZK3kDPIHos1K8M6Ui/NBNmc\n7nGJhOTmoZmmaKniHrdIxevRmgfQnEyhd+E9DOQ5kuUcpaN1Mgm3AgE7JnUG8Pev\njOofihgfKIjM+mEoc1ZcBbRvNE24/zbhdBLY0jySyheor/EViadEYQRJwRznuCak\nrHJtTDLDF7Kw0xe5Nzglnh3Rhg73ZIfoYYWEUT87t7VEzfD8HuSM6XEg7xANDfZU\nfhpS0LWH3Vj0ZG6zs2Y4G9a0GQDz58ehAJhzX57NOKTbSRh1rQKIG77Wj3jT87V0\n+PJyDf45fP+ttusfGDao\n=3zo+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T12:44:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flo