":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/7cd10a63bad232a3c825b69939981262c2d35561/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T19:38:33Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T19:38:33Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: capture every outstanding item as a plan, and guard plan hygiene\n\nThree outstanding items existed ONLY in this conversation and would have died with\nit: the expired Meta token, Google Ads never having run against the real API, and\nthe Desktop path being unverified on an actual Desktop install. They are now\ndocs/plans/live-verification.md, Status: Blocked — each recording what is blocked,\nwhy it cannot proceed here, and the exact commands that unblock it.\n\nTwo plans had no status line at all, and one was actively misleading:\ngoogle-ads-mcp-paid-media-report.md said \"0% (0/17)\" when Phase 1 — the entire\nGoogle Ads MCP — was built this morning. Corrected to 8/17, and given a \"Revised\napproach\" section, because its Phases 2-3 assume a Dapr-and-agents design that\npredates the packages split: the report should be a composition in analytics-core\nthat the analytics skill drives, not an agent pipeline, and the attribution rule\n(never sum platform-reported conversions; Shopify is the source of truth) holds in\neither design.\n\nmarketing-analytics.md is Complete — all 17 steps done — so both it and\ndesktop-consumability.md move to docs/plans/impl/, with their relative links and\ninbound citations rewritten.\n\nAdds check-plans: every plan needs Status: and Established:, a Deferred one needs\nRevisit when:, an archived one needs Lifted to:, a Complete one may not sit in the\nactive directory, and every docs/plans path cited from outside docs/plans must\nresolve. That last rule is the one that bites — archiving a plan silently rots\nevery citation of it. Verified all three fire on deliberate violations.\n\nCLAUDE.md now states the rule this session kept nearly breaking: nothing\noutstanding may live only in a conversation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"f534f5acbe777187f199835a1ccb9c71c7af3a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/f534f5acbe777187f199835a1ccb9c71c7af3a8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/7cd10a63bad232a3c825b69939981262c2d35561","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/7cd10a63bad232a3c825b69939981262c2d35561","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDdjZDEwYTYzYmFkMjMyYTNjODI1YjY5OTM5OTgxMjYyYzJkMzU1NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a","sha":"cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a"}],"sha":"7cd10a63bad232a3c825b69939981262c2d35561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/7cd10a63bad232a3c825b69939981262c2d35561"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T18:10:27Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T18:10:27Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: reconcile the documentation with what the code now does\n\nAn audit for stale claims, dangling links and unrecorded conventions. Everything\nbelow was wrong or missing, not merely improvable.\n\n**Guidance that would have produced the wrong code.** `.claude/rules/mcp-server.md`\nand the `mcp-server` scaffolding skill still emitted `createMcpApp` with no\ntransport selection, no instructions and no prompts — scaffolding a new server\ntoday would have produced something inconsistent with all four analytics servers,\nand HTTP-only. Both now show the `serveMcp` composition root, the steering module,\nand the never-console.log rule that stdio makes load-bearing. The skill also states\nthat logic belongs in `packages/js/<name>-core`, not in the app.\n\n**Dangling links.** README pointed at docs/architecture.html and docs/raw.md, both\ndeleted in an earlier commit and never cleaned up; they now point at\nhow-it-works.md and docs/diagrams/. cc-svc and markdown-mcp linked to ../cc-core\nand ../mcp-core, which moved to packages/js/ in the restructure. Every relative\nlink in every markdown file now resolves, verified with a code-aware checker.\n\n**Stale after the bun switch.** README told users `npm install && npm run dev`;\nthree server READMEs listed Node.js as the prerequisite; the typescript rule said\n`npm run lint`; my own comments in CLAUDE.md and mcp-lifecycle.sh described servers\nrunning as `node dist/index.js`.\n\n**Undocumented conventions.** The six structural guards are now listed in CLAUDE.md\nwith what each catches and why — they are the repo''s contract and were mentioned\nnowhere. README''s package list stopped at mcp-core and now names the five domain\npackages added since.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"fa5d4099b2a130bbfaa52894356bdda34233a5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/fa5d4099b2a130bbfaa52894356bdda34233a5aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGNjNjU0MTMxZjNkY2FiNGQ2ZDFmMjUwMTk0YTg0NWVlYjE5NzU3NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725","sha":"0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725"}],"sha":"cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/cc654131f3dcab4d6d1f250194a845eeb197575a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:21:43Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:21:43Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"fix: wrap an overlong manifest line so lint:md passes\n\nThe previous commit shipped with lint red — the generated diagram''s manifest had a\n261-character line against the 250 limit. Caught by running the gate, not by\nassuming it. lint is green: all six guards, markdown, the diagram drift check and\n23 turbo tasks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"0ebfa5fb0b1611af986b1dbd6801b53a1e7fd17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/0ebfa5fb0b1611af986b1dbd6801b53a1e7fd17c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDBhYzFjMmJmNmFjMzFiOGVlZGZiZmE5ZWQzYzg4NGY1Yzk2YjE3MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380","sha":"138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380"}],"sha":"0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/0ac1c2bf6ac31b8eedfbfa9ed3c884f5c96b1725"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:20:59Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:20:59Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: deliver the diagram check CLAUDE.md already claimed\n\nCLAUDE.md''s Diagrams section stated that `gen-code-diagram --check --dir\ndocs/diagrams` fails the build on drift. It did not: no diagram existed and the\ncheck was in no script. Claiming an enforced convention that is not enforced is\nworse than not having it, since it is read as a guarantee.\n\nAdds docs/diagrams/analytics-mcp-class.md — the shape every analytics MCP server\ntakes, with members extracted from the TypeScript AST — and wires the check into\n`bun run lint`. Verified that a stale generated block fails with a nonzero exit and\na regenerated one passes.\n\nAlso records what the manifest format actually supports, because it cost time to\ndiscover: relations are positional `[from, to, arrow, label]` arrays, `module`\nrequires a `functions` list, and there is no `class` kind — a service is\nrepresented through the port it implements, which is the truer seam anyway.\n\nCorrects docs/plans/effect-ui-api.md, whose status still said ui-api was the only\npackage failing `turbo build`. It compiles as of this morning; the wider migration\n(per-request runPromise, _tag matching at the express boundary) is still open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"c2b0d1818b557ee8a4e450935a1b61f2f951800d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/c2b0d1818b557ee8a4e450935a1b61f2f951800d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDEzOGJmYTY0NTg3NGRlZTEzZWE5OWZkNWJjZjY4NTNiZTNmN2IzODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2","sha":"e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2"}],"sha":"138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/138bfa645874dee13ea99fd5bcf6853be3f7b380"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:13:54Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:13:54Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"chore: complete the bun + uv workspaces, and guard them\n\nBoth workspaces existed; neither was airtight.\n\nuv''s members were hand-listed, so a new Python service joined only if someone\nremembered to add it — the same drift class that left five packages untracked and\nevery MCP image unbuildable. Now globbed, matching the bun side. It cannot be a\nplain `apps/*`: uv errors on a matched directory without a pyproject.toml and most\nof apps/ is TypeScript, so members are `apps/*-worker` and `packages/py/*`. That\nmakes `*-worker` a naming requirement for Python services, now stated in CLAUDE.md.\n\nRemoved apps/ui/src/ui/ — two files, no source, in no workspace, declaring a\ndependency already declared correctly in apps/ui/package.json, and carrying its own\npackage-lock.json inside a bun repo. An artifact of running `vue add quasar` in the\nwrong directory.\n\nAdds check-workspaces: every package.json and pyproject.toml must belong to a\nworkspace or be listed as a deliberate exclusion with a reason, and no\npackage-lock.json / yarn.lock / pnpm-lock.yaml may exist — bun is the only package\nmanager, and a second one silently resolves part of the repo differently. That is\nnot hypothetical: it is exactly how the azdo image ended up unbuildable, with bun\ntolerating a peer conflict npm rejected.\n\nVerified both directions — an orphan manifest and a stray npm lockfile each fail\nthe build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"c4ad04529dec709f777900e1f13ec48fd30cd97d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/c4ad04529dec709f777900e1f13ec48fd30cd97d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGU3ODIwYjE2MTQ0MzM5Mzk3ODhjYWJmNWZjYjdkNjc2MjM1MzhhZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3","sha":"05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3"}],"sha":"e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/e7820b1614433939788cabf5fcb7d67623538ae2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:07:23Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:07:23Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: how it works — primitives, registration lifecycles, flow of a question\n\nExplains what actually happens between a user asking a question in English and a\nnumber coming back: which AI primitives carry intelligence (tools are\nmodel-chosen, prompts user-invoked, instructions server-pushed, skills\ntask-loaded) and why they are not interchangeable — anything that prevents a wrong\nanswer goes in instructions because they are guaranteed to arrive; anything that\nimproves a good answer goes in the skill.\n\nSeparates the three things \"registration\" means, which are routinely conflated:\nbinding a handler at build time, telling a client the server exists at install\ntime, and the handshake that puts capabilities into the model''s context on every\nconnect. That last one is why a code change needs a reconnect and not a restarted\nsession.\n\nThen the request path end to end, with mermaid sequence diagrams — Claude to\npresentation to port to adapter to vendor API and back — including how a failure\ntravels the Effect error channel and arrives as a ToolResult the model can act on\nrather than an exception.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"1dc926458812299ab0403f2485623b1e96c7f0f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/1dc926458812299ab0403f2485623b1e96c7f0f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDA1ZTU1MTJkZDFlOTg5N2ZjMjI3M2YxY2Q1ODJkYzcxNTcxYmRhZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79","sha":"ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79"}],"sha":"05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/05e5512dd1e9897fc2273f1cd582dc71571bdad3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:05:44Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T14:05:44Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"fix: green build, working images, and bun everywhere\n\n**Bugs fixed**\n\n`ui-api` now compiles — `bun run build` is 22/22, green for the first time. It\nfailed on `Effect.fail({ status, message })` with plain objects, which widens the\nerror channel into an un-unifiable union. Replaced with tagged errors (the repo''s\nown Effect rule), adding NotFoundError alongside the existing ForbiddenError, and\nthe catch sites now match on `_tag` instead of a `status` field the errors never\ncarried. Three callbacks also needed explicit return types, because TypeScript\ninfers a flatMap callback from its FIRST return rather than unioning the branches.\n\nEvery MCP image was broken and nothing noticed. Extracting the logic into\npackages/js/* added workspace dependencies that no Dockerfile copied, so the\nimages could not build for two commits — `bun run build` compiles from the\nworkspace on disk and never exercises an image. Fixed, and `check-docker-workspace`\nnow fails lint if an image omits a package its app depends on.\n\nThe same stale NuGet rule that hid five packages from git — `**/packages/*` — was\nalso in .dockerignore, excluding the whole packages tree from every build context.\nScoped to apps/azdoproxy-api in both files.\n\nAll three frontend images were broken too: vis and azdo copied a bun.lockb that is\nnot in their context, ui copied a gitignored .env (which also published config into\nthe served directory), and none had a .dockerignore, so the host node_modules was\ncopied over the freshly-installed one.\n\nPython workers declared `[tool.uv.sources] mndy-framework` but never listed it as a\ndependency, so `uv sync` never installed it and `import mndy_framework` failed in a\nclean environment. It only worked because install.sh was run by hand.\n\n**bun everywhere**\n\nRuntime, package management and builds are now bun, per the repo''s package manager:\n`bun dist/index.js` in every service, bun for the guard scripts, `oven/bun` base\nimages for the frontends and ui-api. This also removed the --legacy-peer-deps\nworkaround the azdo image needed, since bun resolves the nested peers npm could not.\n\npm2 is gone from ui-api — its config was `instances: 1` with autorestart and a\nmemory cap, duplicating what the container runtime already does. `restart:\nunless-stopped` on the compose service preserves the behaviour.\n\nThe Desktop installer now writes an absolute path to bun (Desktop launches with a\nminimal PATH, so a bare `bun` often is not found) plus a `cwd`, so the server also\npicks up its own .env.\n\nImages use `--frozen-lockfile --filter`: all manifests must be present for the\nlockfile to validate, but only this image''s slice installs — without the filter an\nMCP image pulls in Quasar, Vue and the rest of the monorepo.\n\nVerified by actually building and running the images: ga4-mcp and meta-ads-mcp\nbuild, and the container serves MCP over stdio with instructions intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"e1377512fbd81c6337ef71355e00ea08e251abe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/e1377512fbd81c6337ef71355e00ea08e251abe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGVkN2QzNTBjYTlkNDlhMWNmODk1MzkzOGE4YThlYTdkNWIzOGVlNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b","sha":"9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b"}],"sha":"ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/ed7d350ca9d49a1cf8953938a8a8ea7d5b38ee79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:07:29Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:07:29Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"feat: make the analytics MCPs consumable from Claude Desktop\n\nThe audience is shifting from developers driving Claude Code to end users on\nDesktop, and the servers were not usable by them: HTTP-only, so a user had to keep\n`make run-analytics-mcps` in a terminal forever and hand-wire four custom\nconnectors, then separately install steering from a plugin Desktop does not\nconsume.\n\nThree layers, in descending order of leverage:\n\n1. Steering ships INSIDE the servers. Each analytics server now sends\n   `instructions` at initialize and registers prompt starters (\"Meta Ads:\n   performance review\", \"Google Ads: find wasted spend\"). This reaches every MCP\n   client with nothing installed, so the load-bearing rules live there: a null KPI\n   means not-computable rather than zero, money is in the account''s own currency,\n   Shopify is one store per server and is the source of truth for revenue.\n\n2. stdio transport. mcp-core gains `serveMcp`, selecting stdio or HTTP from\n   MCP_TRANSPORT. Desktop spawns the process itself — no port, no lifecycle,\n   nothing to restart after a reboot. HTTP stays for the Claude Code dev loop.\n\n3. An `analytics` skill for what does not fit in instructions: which server\n   answers which question, working across platforms, per-brand targeting, and the\n   attribution trap (platform-reported conversions double-count; never sum them).\n\nPlus `make install-desktop`, which collects credentials and MERGES into\nclaude_desktop_config.json — existing servers preserved, timestamped backup taken.\n\nTwo things caught before shipping:\n\n- `log()` wrote info via console.log. Under stdio that is the JSON-RPC channel,\n  so the first log line would have corrupted the protocol. All logging moves to\n  stderr unconditionally, not by level, so this cannot be reintroduced.\n- Transport inference on \"no TTY\" alone would have flipped detached HTTP servers\n  to stdio, since that runner also redirects stdin from /dev/null. PORT being set\n  keeps them on HTTP. Pinned by a test.\n\nAnd one in the installer: readline/promises leaves a question pending at EOF, so\nwith piped input it exited 0 having silently done nothing. Questions now fail\nloudly, and --yes installs from existing .env files without prompting.\n\nVerified by driving each server exactly as Desktop does — spawning it and speaking\nJSON-RPC over its pipes: clean stdout, instructions delivered, prompts listed,\nlogs on stderr, and the exact command/args/env the installer wrote works.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"82d30f814ad62e5f28c233220bc85daaf40bec26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/82d30f814ad62e5f28c233220bc85daaf40bec26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDkyNTVjZmNiYjBmMmI4ZTJmZTkzNTUwNDM1NDMwNGNmZGQ2ZjU5NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22","sha":"da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22"}],"sha":"9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/9255cfcbb0f2b8e2fe935504354304cfdd6f596b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:46:11Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:46:11Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"feat: check-secrets guard — detect real credentials, ignore placeholders\n\nJudgement proved to be a bad detector: a tracked `.core.env` holding the literal\n`<<azdo-pat>>` was reported as a leaked Azure DevOps PAT needing rotation. It\nwasn''t, and the false alarm cost more than a real finding would have.\n\nMatches on the SHAPE of each provider''s token — prefix, length, alphabet — for\nMeta, Shopify, GitHub, Google, AWS, Slack, private-key blocks and Azure DevOps,\nthen discards anything visibly filler (a run of one repeated character, or a\nstand-in word like \"your\"/\"example\"). Verified both directions: a real-shaped\nghp_ token fails the build, while ghp_xxxx…, <<azdo-pat>> and\nshpat_your_token_here do not.\n\nScans tracked files in the working tree, not history — the point is to stop the\nnext leak, and rewriting history is almost never the right response to an old one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"c38db92d13ec26134b45e67fd4f26886079d2703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/c38db92d13ec26134b45e67fd4f26886079d2703"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGRhMGVhMzhlYmU0YWY3MDRlNDIzMmZjMTExYjEyNzYzODI0NzFhMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a","sha":"168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a"}],"sha":"da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/da0ea38ebe4af704e4232fc111b1276382471a22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:12:36Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:12:36Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: correct the false credential-leak claim\n\n`src/.core.env` held `<<azdo-pat>>` — a placeholder in this repo''s own `<<...>>`\ntemplate convention, 12 characters where a real BASE64_AZDO_PAT would be ~72 of\nbase64 and would decode. I reported it as a committed credential requiring\nrotation; commits 101c389 and 682ff3e state that, and it is wrong.\n\nVerified properly this time: all 1,570 blobs in history scanned against markers\nfor Meta, Shopify, GitHub, GCP, Google, AWS, Slack and Azure DevOps tokens. The\nonly hit was `ghp_xxxxxxxx...` in github-issues-mcp/.env.template, likewise a\nplaceholder. There are no real credentials in this repository''s history, nothing\nto rotate, and no reason to rewrite history.\n\nRemoves the bogus \"Rotate the Azure DevOps PAT\" follow-up, annotates the finding\nin the archived plan, and rewords the .gitignore comment.\n\nThe ignore-rule fix itself stands: `**/.env` genuinely does not match dotted\nvariants like `.core.env`, so a real one would have been committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"57426ec1ea2c2a3fcf7efbc98dc3394cf44712a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/57426ec1ea2c2a3fcf7efbc98dc3394cf44712a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDE2OGEzYjBlNjFkYjYwYjg4ZjdiODIwNzY3ZmE1OTE5OWQwMmYwMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640","sha":"5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640"}],"sha":"168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/168a3b0e61db60b88f7b820767fa59199d02f00a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:02:09Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:02:09Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"feat: detached MCP lifecycle so code changes land without restarting Claude\n\nAnswers \"can I rebuild and use the change in the same session?\" — yes, and this\nmakes the loop graceful:\n\n    # edit code\n    make restart-analytics-mcps\n    # in Claude Code: /mcp -> reconnect\n\nVerified end to end by changing a tool description, restarting, and reusing the\nsame MCP session id: without reconnecting the call fails with `400 Bad Request:\nServer not initialized`, and after re-running the handshake it returns 200 with\nthe NEW description. createMcpApp builds a fresh McpServer per session, so new\ntools, renames and schema changes all appear on reconnect. Restarting the Claude\nsession is never needed.\n\nrun-analytics-mcps still exists but is foreground-only, so it cannot be restarted\nwithout dropping the shell. Adds start/stop/restart/status/logs targets backed by\nscripts/mcp-lifecycle.sh.\n\nThe script identifies a server by the working directory of its process\n(/proc/<pid>/cwd) rather than its command line, because every server runs as\n`node dist/index.js` and the command line cannot tell them apart. That matters:\nthe first cut of these targets used pidfiles alone, and an orphan surviving from\nan earlier run kept holding port 3005 — the new instance died on EADDRINUSE, the\npidfile pointed at nothing, and `status` reported \"up\" because the orphan was\nanswering the health check. It now reports ORPHAN and `stop` reaps it.\n\nstart also refuses a port already in use rather than launching a doomed process,\nwaits for /health before claiming success, and skips a server with no .env with a\nmessage instead of crash-looping it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"3d9211324ed492871792b1c23e0b9df53cef4b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/3d9211324ed492871792b1c23e0b9df53cef4b01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDUzMTdmZGFmODc5NGIxMmY2YjFlM2ZkZTBkYTQ3MTRiMzMzMDE2NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30","sha":"682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30"}],"sha":"5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/5317fdaf8794b12f6b1e3fde0da4714b33301640"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:21:09Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:21:09Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"fix: five packages were never committed, and Meta retried expired tokens\n\nFound by actually running the servers against live credentials.\n\n**The packages/ tree was gitignored.** .gitignore carried the stock NuGet rule\n`**/packages/*`, which silently swallowed the workspace directory created in the\nrestructure. analytics-core, ga4-core and google-ads-core had ZERO tracked files;\ngithub-core, meta-ads-core and shopify-core had only the one file each that git mv\nhad carried over already tracked. The previous two commits were therefore\nincomplete and a fresh clone could not build — it worked locally only because the\nfiles existed on disk. The rule is now scoped to apps/azdoproxy-api, the one C#\nproject that has a NuGet restore folder.\n\n**Meta retried expired-token failures.** isRetryableError treats a missing error\ncode as \"unknown, therefore transient\", and the SDK surfaces an expired token with\na readable message and no code — so every doomed call was retried three times with\nexponential backoff. A live call took 8218ms to tell us the token expired in\nMarch; the integration suite took 72.8s to report the same thing six times.\n\nAdds MetaAuthError with a pure isAuthFailure classifier matching on both code 190\nand the message forms Meta actually uses, excluded from the retry predicate and\nsurfaced with an actionable message naming the fix. Same call now fails in 420ms\nand the suite runs in 3.2s.\n\nAlso adds packages/js/mcp-core/src/runtime.test.ts, which pins the shared-runtime\nfix from the previous commit: 5 tool calls build the client once through\ncreateServerRuntime and five times through the old\nEffect.runPromise(provide(...)) idiom, kept as an executable record of why the\nruntime exists. The Effect validator hook now exempts *.test.ts, since a\nregression test''s job is to exercise the anti-pattern it guards against.\n\n.turbo/ is gitignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"09d78591097364312b87ecba294e891e4e23ffbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/09d78591097364312b87ecba294e891e4e23ffbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDY4MmZmM2U4NjIzMWNmNzM0ODMxNWJiNzAwZmUyMGZkMzhlYTRiMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7","sha":"2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7"}],"sha":"682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/682ff3e86231cf7348315bb700fe20fd38ea4b30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:48:12Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:48:12Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: archive the monorepo-maturity plan\n\nAll five parts are Complete, so the plan moves to docs/plans/impl/ as a unit per\nthe plan-management lifecycle.\n\nBefore archiving, every piece of lasting context was lifted to its one long-lived\nhome — the plan''s README now carries the \"Lifted to\" table naming each\ndestination: CLAUDE.md for the packages/apps principle, the modes and the plan\nand diagram conventions; .claude/rules/mcp-server.md for the zod-at-the-boundary\nand shared-runtime decisions; analytics-core for the KPI and anomaly maths that\nused to be prose; and the three check-*.mjs guards for the invariants. Parked\nitems live in docs/plans/carried-followups.md.\n\nCitations into the plan were rewritten in the same change, and every relative\nlink in and out of the moved directory verified to resolve.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"5c2ea51137c12c473ed855d9dce4e384fd2fd1c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/5c2ea51137c12c473ed855d9dce4e384fd2fd1c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDJjNmMxMjk1MzAyMzEwYTEzYTlkOWQ1OTVhODdlNWMzMGUyNjMzYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1","sha":"63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1"}],"sha":"2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/2c6c1295302310a13a9d9d595a87e5c30e2633a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:46:08Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:46:08Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: make analytics-MCP mode the front door, and guard the claim\n\nThe most-used thing this repo produces is a handful of analytics MCP servers\nthat need no infrastructure at all. That was true before this commit but was\ndocumented as an aside — a qualification buried inside the full-platform setup,\nso a reader met Dapr, MongoDB and RabbitMQ before reaching \"actually you need\nnone of this\".\n\nREADME now opens with the two modes and gives Mode 1 a complete\nclone-to-first-tool-call path that mentions Dapr exactly once, to say you do not\nneed it. Quick Start is retitled \"Quick Start (full platform)\".\n\nWhich servers need infrastructure is now stated in ONE place — a table in the\nREADME — and CLAUDE.md, the plugin README and the mndy-mcps skill link to it\ninstead of each paraphrasing it slightly differently. CLAUDE.md gains a Modes\nsection with the operational instruction: a question about GA4/Meta/Google\nAds/Shopify data is Mode 1, so don''t send the user to stand up infrastructure and\ndon''t run `make install` when `bun install` is enough.\n\nProse cannot hold an invariant, so scripts/check-mcp-parity.mjs now enforces it:\nevery MCP app must have a package.json, .env.template with a port, README, make\ntarget and a row in the README table; every port the plugin registers must be\nserved by some app; and a server documented as infrastructure-free must not\ndepend on Dapr. It found a real gap immediately — apps/dapr-mcp had no README.\n\nAlso clears the 94 markdown-lint issues deferred from the first commit and adds\nlint:md to `bun run lint`. `make lint-md` passes for the first time in this\nrepo''s history; it had sat at 714 errors with no config file, which is why nobody\nran it. MD024 was fixed by configuration (siblings_only) rather than by mangling\nreference docs where a repeated subheading under a different parent is correct.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"c4a8e2e43a7a6d56c8b75e0e0607c76328131bff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/c4a8e2e43a7a6d56c8b75e0e0607c76328131bff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDYzNzUzZjJjOTUyYTQxZmMxZGZlYzU1Y2IzMmMyYjMzZWE5YjNjYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7","sha":"f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7"}],"sha":"63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/63753f2c952a41fc1dfec55cb32c2b33ea9b3cb1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:37:48Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:37:48Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"feat: google-ads-mcp — paid search/display as a first-class analytics MCP\n\nGoogle Ads was the last gap in the paid-media picture: Meta, GA4 and Shopify were\ncovered, and apps/google-ads-mcp held a single orphaned types.ts that was in no\nworkspace and had never been built.\n\n  packages/js/google-ads-core   domain + Google Ads API adapter (17 tests)\n  apps/google-ads-mcp           container on port 3010\n\nTwo tools, both taking a per-call customerId so one running server serves every\nbrand: google_ads_get_performance (spend, impressions, clicks, conversions,\nrevenue + ROAS/CPA/CTR/CVR/CPC/CPM from analytics-core) and\ngoogle_ads_get_campaigns.\n\nUnlike the other platforms, GAQL query construction is real domain logic — which\nfields each aggregation level needs, which quality metrics exist at which level —\nso it lives in domain/ and is tested rather than buried in the adapter.\n\nNotable specifics:\n\n- The orphaned scaffolding defaulted to PORT 3006, which is dapr-mcp''s. It was\n  invisible to every build, so nothing caught it. Now 3010, covered by\n  check-ports.mjs.\n- Auth and quota failures do NOT retry. A test-level developer token will never\n  succeed and Google Ads quotas are daily, so backing off just delays the real\n  error; the quota message tells the agent so explicitly.\n- Cost micros are converted exactly once, in the adapter. analytics-core''s\n  normalizer also knows about micros, so the call site notes why it sums the\n  adapter''s spend directly rather than dividing by a million twice.\n- Campaign IDs from tool input are filtered to numerics before being interpolated\n  into GAQL.\n\nWired into make run-google-ads-mcp and run-analytics-mcps, the plugin''s .mcp.json,\na new google-ads skill, the brands skill and registry template\n(googleAdsCustomerId), and CLAUDE.md.\n\nlint 23/23 and test 13/13 (53 tests) pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"d3f9b982076123f309e0c693361e9ddd138bd490","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/d3f9b982076123f309e0c693361e9ddd138bd490"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGYzZTI0NjcwYzcyMzE4ODJjYjhjMGFiM2JmNTljZmRmYWFiODdlYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3","sha":"fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3"}],"sha":"f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/f3e24670c7231882cb8c0ab3bf59cfdfaab87eb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:30:14Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:30:14Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"refactor: move MCP logic into packages, servers become containers\n\nApplies the principle now stated in CLAUDE.md: reusable machinery lives in\npackages/, and an MCP server is a container around it — config, tool schemas,\nregistration, composition root, nothing more.\n\nFive new packages under packages/js/:\n\n  analytics-core   the pure cross-platform domain — canonical metric vocabulary,\n                   KPI math, anomaly thresholds, brand registry, money/timezone.\n                   31 tests. No I/O.\n  ga4-core         GA4 domain + Data API adapter\n  meta-ads-core    Meta domain + Marketing API adapter (5 tests)\n  shopify-core     Shopify domain + Admin API adapter\n  github-core      GitHub issues domain + REST adapter\n\nga4-mcp, meta-ads-mcp, shopify-mcp and github-issues-mcp are now containers: no\nvendor SDK appears in any app''s dependencies. dapr-mcp gets the runtime fix and\nthe presentation layer; its logic extraction is carried forward.\n\nThree real bugs surfaced on the way:\n\n- Every tool call was building a new platform client. The idiom\n  `Effect.runPromise(effect.pipe(Effect.provide(Service.Default)))` builds the\n  layer while executing and makes a fresh runtime per call, so each request\n  constructed a new GA4 client / Octokit / Shopify session, discarding pools and\n  redoing auth. mcp-core gains createServerRuntime (ManagedRuntime, built once),\n  which also gives the servers a real shutdown path.\n\n- The \"never use zod\" rule was unachievable — the MCP SDK accepts only zod for\n  inputSchema — and the workaround was worse than either option: every analytics\n  server declared its tool input twice, once in zod for the SDK and once in a\n  dead Effect Schema that had already drifted. The rule now says what is true:\n  zod is an inbound-adapter concern confined to presentation/.\n\n- meta_get_insights prefixed its spend total with a literal \"$\" regardless of the\n  ad account''s currency, which is wrong for every ZAR account. Totals now come\n  from analytics-core and carry no symbol.\n\nAlso fixes .claude/hooks/effect-validator.sh, which flagged Effect.tryPromise —\nthe correct idiom — as a JS try/catch and would have blocked most of this work,\nand drops ui-api''s default `exit 1` test script that failed turbo test.\n\nbun run lint (guards + 20 tasks) and bun run test (36 tests) pass. bun run build\nis 15/20, unchanged: only the pre-existing ui-api failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"fb86c7408eb9ed3dbe2e2c2ab3d0033a3bb0c5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/fb86c7408eb9ed3dbe2e2c2ab3d0033a3bb0c5f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGZiNGZiMWFhZGQ1YjI5ZGRlZDkxMjg0ZGYyNzYyZDRmZmJmODhmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e","sha":"101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e"}],"sha":"fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/fb4fb1aadd5b29dded91284df2762d4ffbf88fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:04:31Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:04:31Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"refactor: restructure into an apps/ + packages/ monorepo, following h\n\nsrc/ is gone. Everything now sits where its role says it should:\n\n  apps/         things you run (frontends, workers, services, MCP servers)\n  packages/js/  TypeScript libraries — the reusable machinery\n  packages/py/  mndy-framework\n  config/       Dapr components, wiremock mappings\n  tools/        loose scripts and sandboxes\n\nWorkspaces are glob-based (apps/*, packages/js/*, scripts), so adding a package\nno longer means editing a 16-entry list. Adds turbo for build/lint/test\norchestration, .dependency-cruiser.cjs carrying the hex boundary rules, and two\nguards in scripts/: check-ports.mjs and check-hex-lint.mjs.\n\nThe move uncovered six latent breakages, all fixed here except where noted:\n\n- src/.core.env was TRACKED IN GIT and holds a BASE64_AZDO_PAT. .gitignore''s\n  `**/.env` matches only files named exactly .env, never dotted variants. Ignore\n  rule fixed and the file untracked — but the PAT is still in history and needs\n  rotating.\n- The four `make run-*-worker` targets passed --resources-path\n  ../../dapr/components.local/, a directory that has never existed in this repo.\n  Now points at components.localhost, which is what the other Dapr targets use.\n- Every root-context Dockerfile copied bun.lockb; bun 1.3 writes bun.lock.\n- ui-api and github-issues-mcp both defaulted to port 3001 and so could never run\n  together. github-issues-mcp moves to 3009 (plugin .mcp.json, compose, skills,\n  docs and tests all follow), and check-ports.mjs makes a recurrence a lint error.\n- apps/vis, apps/azdo and apps/markdown-mcp declared lint scripts that could not\n  execute. Removed — false coverage is worse than none; real coverage lands with\n  the depcruise work.\n- uv.lock cannot re-resolve once its members point at missing directories, so its\n  paths were rewritten by hand.\n\nVerified: make build-mcp, build-dapr, build-cc-svc, uv lock/sync and bun run lint\nall pass. turbo build is 10/15 — apps/ui-api fails on pre-existing Effect type\nerrors, confirmed by diffing its sources byte-for-byte against HEAD. That belongs\nto docs/plans/effect-ui-api.md.\n\nParked items are collected in docs/plans/carried-followups.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"41910a6c6a38208bd7930fd33dfab32d55b6ebda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/41910a6c6a38208bd7930fd33dfab32d55b6ebda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKDEwMWMzODlkZGRmZTNkYTdlYTc4NTQ0ZGZkZGNmNDYwNDU5Mzc0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9","sha":"d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9"}],"sha":"101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/101c389dddfe3da7ea78544dfddcf4604593744e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T08:49:19Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T08:49:19Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"chore: adopt the shared Claude Code plugins and the plan/diagram conventions\n\nWires mndy into the same plugin set h uses, so the conventions live in installed\nplugins rather than in prose duplicated across steering files:\n\n- effect-claude-primitives (Effect-TS patterns)\n- hex-arch (ports-and-adapters layering)\n- plan-management (plan doc lifecycle)\n- code-comprehension (generated code diagrams)\n- c4-mermaid-plugin (authored C4 views)\n\neffect-primitives resolves through a user-level directory marketplace, matching h,\nso it is enabled but not declared project-side; the other four are GitHub sources\nand come with a fresh clone. @stiproot/code-comprehension is also a root\ndevDependency so CI gets the gen-code-diagram binary.\n\nCLAUDE.md gains Plans, Diagrams and \"Where code lives\" sections. The last states\nthe principle the rest of this effort follows: reusable machinery lives in\npackages/, and MCP servers and services are containers around it.\n\nAlso makes the markdown gate real. lint-md had no config at all, so it ran on\nstrict 80-column defaults and reported 714 errors — unpassable, therefore unrun.\nAdds the house-style .markdownlint.yml plus an ignore file and applies --fix,\nleaving 94 genuine content issues for the doc-hardening phase.\n\nThe whole effort is planned in docs/plans/monorepo-maturity/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KSbSgPgqjmKMS8MwFCobVm","tree":{"sha":"d5b9aac23e654699b4eab0bf1ae7a47edfa92524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/d5b9aac23e654699b4eab0bf1ae7a47edfa92524"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9","node_id":"C_kwDOQOHO_doAKGQ0NGMzZDExNTJhNDc0NzNlMjI4MTlhNDY4NzkzM2Q2NDcxNzgwYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot/mndy/commit/485dc823a3ca5948e17cde0e076ab17f98b54c5f","sha":"485dc823a3ca5948e17cde0e076ab17f98b54c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/485dc823a3ca5948e17cde0e076ab17f98b54c5f"}],"sha":"d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/d44c3d1152a47473e22819a4687933d6471780a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/commits/485dc823a3ca5948e17cde0e076ab17f98b54c5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T14:57:31Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T14:57:31Z","email":"stipcich.simon@gmail.com","name":"stiproot"},"message":"docs: update steering context for the analytics MCPs and brand switching\n\nThe plugin-side skills documented brand switching, but the repo-side steering\nnever caught up — and some of it was wrong.\n\n- marketing-agent skill: the MCP tool examples did not match the real schemas.\n  Corrected property_id -> propertyId, date_preset -> datePreset, GA4''s flat\n  start_date/end_date -> dateRanges: [{startDate, endDate}], and metrics/\n  dimensions -> arrays of {name} objects. Added the missing adAccountId and a\n  note that GA4/Meta are camelCase while Shopify is snake_case.\n- marketing-analytics rules: document per-call account targeting as a required\n  pattern (targeting is per call, never a mutable field on a service), the\n  Shopify single-store exception, and the gitignored brand registry.\n- CLAUDE.md: list the analytics/dapr/markdown/google-ads MCP servers with their\n  ports (only mcp-core and github-issues were listed), add their make targets,\n  and point at the brand registry.\n\nAlso fixes two inaccuracies found while verifying the above:\n\n- make help advertised port 3001 for both ga4-mcp and shopify-mcp; they listen\n  on 3003 and 3005.\n- the help target''s grep excluded digits, so run-ga4-mcp, test-ga4-mcp, and\n  test-cc-svc-brand-e2e never appeared in `make help`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac5e84b3d82cb7cd903ed2a7affcc309d262de20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/trees/ac5e84b3d82cb7cd903ed2a7affcc309d262de20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiproot/mndy/git/commits/485dc823a3ca5948e17cde0e076ab17f98b54c5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95277988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stiproot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stiproot","id":95277988,"login":"stiproot","node_id":"U_kgDOBa3TpA",